            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Georgia"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This lemonade is a great addition to any gathering. I use Splenda instead of sugar and it's just as good. Thank you for this refreshing drink.",
            "datePublished": "2008-08-12T10:19:02.390Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kim Snyder"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a really good tart-sweet lemonade. We have juiced a bunch of lemons and are now freezing the juice in 2cup measures just to make this!",
            "datePublished": "2010-02-19T13:00:09.790Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Brian Konrad"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Just a side note: it is a lot easier to combine the sugar with the rest of the ingredients if you do it this way:\n\n1. Place sugar in small sauce pan\n2. Add a cup of water for 1.5 cups sugar. Thus recipe calls for 2 cups sugar. Maybe 1 3/4 cups water with that. \n3. Bring to a boil while stirring to make a thin syrup. \n4. Reduce heat and keep stirring as needed to dissolve all sugar\n5. Remove from heat, allow to cool, cover saucepan and place in fridge to chill. \n\nWhen the time comes to use the sugar, just pour in the syrup and mix.",
            "datePublished": "2020-07-26T02:24:59.717Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mother Ann"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My son is a huge pink lemonade fan, so I made this for him to try. He gave it 2 thumbs up! We didn't use quite 2 cups of sugar as he likes his less sweet. Sure hits the spot!",
            "datePublished": "2011-02-21T07:45:32.993Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Angelica Zaldivar"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is sweeter than I prefer my lemonade, but a base recipe! I love to eat lemons like apples, so as you can imagine I like my lemonade tart. The first time I made it I used 2 cups frozen raspberries and blended them with 2 cups water to make 'raspberry juice'. i strained it and used that in place of the cranberry -- it was a huge hit. I also took the sugar down to 1 1/2 cups. The next time I made it i used frozen strawberries. Because they are so sweet, and I had made a bigger batch i did the following: 1 1/2 c frozen strawberries, 14 cups water, 1 1/2 c sugar and 4 c lemon juice. it was perfect! I had a bbq yesterday with about 15 people total and ended up making 6 GALLONS of this in 2 hours!",
            "datePublished": "2013-01-21T14:05:31.430Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "leasophia"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Refreshing! I doubled the recipe, made simple syrup (as suggested) and because I used very sweet Meyer lemons from my tree, I added two more to “tart” it up a bit. Simple and delicious",
            "datePublished": "2019-03-30T21:49:19.747Z"
          },
          {
